**How to implement.** The constructor window runs a study's fit off the UI thread through a job host its shell carries, and a completed fit's run joins the window's history at once (001 §N 'Long fits run on `JobRunner`, with progress and cancel; the fit run is written on completion'; 001 §P `RunFit`; .spec-md §10.2 'one fit iteration … a progress bar with Cancel, through `JobRunner`', §10.3 'Fits … are one click with Cancel', §10.4 'The job's completion message updates the Elmish model, so the fit-run history, the results tabs … re-render without a manual reload'). It hosts S11.3's fit job (`StudyFitJob.fs`, step 393) as Send kit hosts its archive job (steps 200, 201): the host in the shell, the state in the model, the message wrapping `StudyFitMsg`. Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S11.5. (1) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/StudyFitJob.fs`: `StudyFitJobHost` (step 393) gains `static member inert : StudyFitJobHost`, which runs nothing and answers a handle that does nothing, `KitArchiveJobHost.inert`'s shape (step 200): the default of a scene that runs no fit. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs`. (a) `KitWindowShell` (steps 186, 201) gains `studyFits : StudyFitJobHost`, documented in one line; `KitWindowShell.inert` holds `StudyFitJobHost.inert`, so every shell built as an update of `inert` keeps its behaviour until the windows compose the real host (step 419). (b) `TableAndElementRotationModel` gains `studyFit : StudyFitJobState` (step 393) after `studySurface` (step 410), documented in one line; `initWith` sets `StudyFitJobState.idle`. (c) On the model extension holding `studyContext` (step 410): `member model.studyForwardContext : StudyForwardContext` (step 372) = `{ kit = model.studyContext; library = model.library; materials = model.materials; experimentData = model.experimentData; choiceOf = model.tryItemModelChoice; solverParameters = SolverParameters.defaultValue }` (`Berreman/Berreman/Solvers.fs:SolverParameters.defaultValue`), documented in one line. (d) `TableAndElementRotationMsg` gains `StudyFit of StudyFitMsg`, documented in one line: the Fit step's verbs and the fit job's own progress and end. (e) The arm. `StudyFit (RunFit _)` goes through step 185's read-only guard first, because a fit writes its fit run (step 384). Every `StudyFit msg` is then `msg.updateWith (StudyFitEnvironment.create model.kitShell.studyFits model.kit.proxy model.studyForwardContext model.kit.clock) model.studyFit` (step 393), the model taking the answered state: one fit at a time, the run written on completion only, nothing on cancel or error. After `StudyFitEnded (Ok run)`, when the answered state's job is `Completed` with `committedResults = Some run.name` (`JobRunner.fs:JobModel`) and its `errorOpt` is `None`, `kitFitRuns` gains `run` at its end and `studySurface.fitRunOpt` becomes `Some run.name`, so the history and the results show it with no reload; when the kit refused it (`FitRunKitErr`), the error stays in the state for the Fit step to show (step 415) and `kitFitRuns` is unchanged. No queue, retry, second job or option is added. Tests, in `StudyWindowModelTests` (step 410), the shell's `studyFits` being either `StudyFitJobHost.posting` whose `post` calls at once and whose `progressed` and `ended` record `StudyFit (StudyFitProgressed _)` and `StudyFit (StudyFitEnded _)`, which the fact passes back through `updateTableAndElementRotation` in order after waiting on a `ManualResetEventSlim` with a ten-second limit, never a sleep (`StudyFitJobTests`' host, step 393), or a test-local host record whose `startStudyFit` records the job and answers a handle that records its cancel. `RunFit starts one fit through the shell's host, Cancel cancels it, and a read-only kit starts none`: with `QZ-LR` over E1 and E2, `StudyFit (RunFit { study = QZ-LR; stage = JointStage; calibrationUse = CalibrationHeldFixed })` over the recording host leaves `studyFit.job.isRunning` and one recorded job; a second `RunFit` records none; `StudyFit CancelStudyFit` records the cancel; over the kit opened read-only the guard refuses `RunFit` and no job is recorded. `a fit's end writes its fit run into the kit and shows it in the history at once`: after a recorded start, `StudyFit (StudyFitEnded (Ok <a test-local fit run of QZ-LR>))` leaves `readFitRuns QZ-LR` answering the run, `kitFitRuns` ending with it and `studySurface.fitRunOpt` naming it; the same end when the kit already holds that run leaves `kitFitRuns` unchanged and `studyFit.errorOpt` holding `FitRunKitErr (FitRunExistsErr _)`. `a fit that cannot run tells why and writes nothing`: over the posting host, after `StudyCommand (CreateStudy (Empty, []))`, `RunFit` of `Empty`, a study of no experiment, ends with `studyFit.errorOpt` holding `FitStageErr (NoStageRunErr _)` (step 385), the job not running and the kit holding no `.fitrun-json`. All choice construction and matching in this step MUST use step 216's payloads, including the resolved ItemModelVersion for source, ideal-polarizer and stack choices. Fixtures MUST obtain those versions from step 210's shipped model entries; runtime resolution MUST use the stored version through ItemModelProxy, never manufacture a model or use a preset/sample as the model. Existing parameter values and optical results MUST be preserved.

**Acceptance.** After the fit is hosted, `StudyFit` MUST run a study's fit through the shell's `StudyFitJobHost` over `model.studyForwardContext`, refused under a read-only kit, and a completed fit's run MUST join `kitFitRuns` and be chosen with no reload while an error stays in `studyFit`; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `RunFit starts one fit through the shell's host, Cancel cancels it, and a read-only kit starts none`, `a fit's end writes its fit run into the kit and shows it in the history at once` and `a fit that cannot run tells why and writes nothing`, the count rising by 3; ui-smoke MUST pass; and build, elevation and the twenty s40 invariants MUST pass.
